Companion code change for supabase/migrations/0105_external_ref_canonical_card.sql
==================================================================================

Apply BOTH or NEITHER, in the same deploy. Three edits, all in
packages/shared/src/efsImport/parse.ts. Each makes the leading <card> segment of an
external_ref the card's LAST 4 DIGITS, so a file import (masked card) and the SOAP
feed (full card number) produce the SAME ref for the same transaction.

Add to the imports at the top of the file:

    import { cardLast4 } from "../cardAssignment.js";

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1) normalizeTransactionRows — the merged fuel events (fuel_transactions.external_ref)

   Move the cardRefVal line ABOVE the `card` line, then:

-  const card = cardShort ?? cardFull;
-  const cardRefVal =
-    [cardFull, cardShort].filter((v): v is string => !!v).sort((a, b) => b.length - a.length)[0] ?? card;
+  const cardRefVal =
+    [cardFull, cardShort].filter((v): v is string => !!v).sort((a, b) => b.length - a.length)[0] ??
+    (cardShort ?? cardFull);
+  // Canonical ref segment: the last 4 digits — the ONLY form both the masked file report and the
+  // full-number SOAP feed can produce for the same card. Keeps one transaction to one external_ref
+  // regardless of which channel delivered it. See migration 0105.
+  const card = cardLast4(cardRefVal) ?? cardShort ?? cardFull;

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2) normalizeAllTransactionLines — the faithful store (efs_transactions.external_ref)

   `card` is used BOTH for the ref and for the stored card_num. Only the ref changes:

   const card = str(pick(row, "Card #", "Card Number"));
+  const refCard = cardLast4(card) ?? card;   // canonical ref segment (migration 0105)

   ...then in the returned object:

-    external_ref: txnId
-      ? [card ?? "", txnId, item ?? "", qty ?? "", amt ?? "", instant?.tranDate ?? ""].join("|")
-      : [card ?? "", invoice ?? "", item ?? "", qty ?? "", amt ?? "", instant?.tranDate ?? ""].join("|"),
+    external_ref: txnId
+      ? [refCard ?? "", txnId, item ?? "", qty ?? "", amt ?? "", instant?.tranDate ?? ""].join("|")
+      : [refCard ?? "", invoice ?? "", item ?? "", qty ?? "", amt ?? "", instant?.tranDate ?? ""].join("|"),

   (card_num keeps the verbatim value — the faithful store must stay faithful.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3) deriveFuelEventsFromEfsStore — re-derivation from the faithful store

-  const dateKey = `${str(l.card_num) ?? ""}|${invoice}|${l.tran_date}`;
+  // Must match normalizeTransactionRows byte-for-byte or a re-derive creates duplicates.
+  const dateKey = `${cardLast4(l.card_num) ?? str(l.card_num) ?? ""}|${invoice}|${l.tran_date}`;

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Verification after applying both

  * `pnpm --filter @fuelguard/shared test` — efsImport.test.ts asserts on external_ref values and
    WILL fail until its expected refs are updated to the last-4 form. That failure is the intended
    signal, not a regression: update the fixtures to match.
  * Re-import a file you have already imported. Expect `duplicate_rows` to equal the row count and
    `newFuel` to be 0. If you see new rows, code and data are out of sync — stop and re-check.
  * Only then enable the SOAP feed.
